Sources for `brainstorming` skill (see plans/skill-audits/brainstorming.md for full audit):

- superpowers/brainstorming — primary source. Hard gate, one-question, multi-choice preferred, 2–3 approaches, spec-write, transition to writing-plans.
- gstack /office-hours — composed upstream (validates the IDEA before brainstorming the implementation).
- compound-engineering (EveryInc) — plan phase referenced; rejected as primary (no clear gate between explore and implement).
- Boris Cherny "how Boris uses Claude Code" — discipline of writing the design before code.

Strategy: distill. Three deliberate changes from superpowers:
1. Spec location: docs/specs/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>.md (consumer convention)
2. Transition target: voidcorp:writing-plans (vendored equivalent)
3. No trigger filter on activation (per Section 0bis hedge resolution)

No companion hooks; the gate is a process discipline enforced via code-review flags downstream.
